EXT. SNOWBOUND MOUNTAIN PASS - DAY

Wind-scoured white. A crashed bus lies on its side, half-buried in drift.

Six survivors huddle in its lee. GLORIA PENDERGAST (50s), the driver, scrapes ice off a window. DANIEL HOYT (30s) feeds a tiny fire. SUNITA RAO (40s) bandages a boy's hand. The boy, TEDDY (9), watches the flames. AUGUST LEBLANC (60s) and his wife COLETTE (60s) share one blanket.

She tucks Teddy's scarf tighter. He doesn't flinch.

GLORIA
Radio's dead.

DANIEL
Of course it is.

SUNITA
We have food for two days.

AUGUST
Three, if we ration.

COLETTE
Four, if we don't mind being hungry.

He hands her the last cracker. She breaks it in half and gives one piece to the boy.

TEDDY
Thank you.

She nods. Gloria sets her jaw, picks up a shovel, and heads into the wind. He rises to follow. She waves him back.

GLORIA
Stay. Keep the fire.

Daniel sits. Sunita looks at the sky. Nobody says a word.
